{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.KnotEigenbasisComplete","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.KnotEigenbasisComplete","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":74,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.single_summand_detected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.single_summand_detected","kind":"theorem","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L417-L431","doc":"**The Jones value of some closure is non-zero**, for a single-block\ndecomposition — obtained by composing summand detection with the trace\ndecomposition rather than by re-exporting a field.\n\nThis is the statement `knot_eigenbasis_density` appeared to make and did\nnot: it concerns `markov.tr`, the quantity the manuscript identifies with\nthe Jones polynomial of the closure, and it is *proved* from the block\ndetection rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.tr_ne_zero_of_single_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.tr_ne_zero_of_single_block","kind":"theorem","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L403-L415","doc":"**A non-zero block component is visible in the total trace when the\ndecomposition has a single block** — *derived* from `tr_eq_sum_blocks`,\nwhich is the constraint the old encoding had no analogue of.\n\nFor `n ≤ 1` the Schur–Weyl decomposition has `⌊n/2⌋ + 1 = 1` partition,\nso the whole Markov trace is that one block's component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.eigenbasis_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.eigenbasis_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L393-L401","doc":"**Corollary**: The eigenbasis is non-empty when V^⊗n has\nat least one irreducible summand (which holds for all n ≥ 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.knot_eigenbasis_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.knot_eigenbasis_complete","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L374-L391","doc":"**Theorem (Knot eigenbasis completeness).**\nGiven the three components of KnotEigenbasisData, every element of\nV^⊗n belongs to an irreducible summand that is detected by a\nknot type (braid closure).\n\nThis is the combining step: Schur–Weyl provides the decomposition,\nAlexander provides the braid representative, and the Markov trace\nconfirms detection. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete","label":"prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.summands_detected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.summands_detected","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L369-L369","doc":"**Summand detection**: for each partition μ in the decomposition,\nthere exists a braid β whose Markov trace **in the block `S_μ`** is\nnon-zero — i.e. the Jones polynomial of the closure β̂, restricted to\nthat summand, does not vanish.\n\n`μ` occurs in the body. The previous version bound it and did not,\nwhich `mu_free_detection_vacuous` above shows says nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.tr_eq_sum_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.tr_eq_sum_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L359-L359","doc":"The block components decompose the trace:\n`tr x = Σ_{μ ∈ partitions} trBlock μ x`.\n\nThis is what stops `trBlock` from being free data an instance may\nchoose independently of `markov.tr`, and it is what\n`tr_ne_zero_of_single_block` is proved from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.trBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.trBlock","kind":"def","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L352-L352","doc":"Component of the Markov trace in the block `S_μ`.\n\nWithout this the decomposition is invisible to the trace and no\nstatement can be made *per summand* — see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.braid_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.braid_rep","kind":"def","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L347-L347","doc":"Representation map: braid → Hecke algebra element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.markov","kind":"def","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L345-L345","doc":"Part 3: Markov trace (parameterized by H, no type equality needed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.alex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.alex","kind":"def","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L343-L343","doc":"Part 2: Alexander surjectivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.decomp_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.decomp_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L341-L341","doc":"Consistency: decomposition uses the same Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.decomp","kind":"def","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L339-L339","doc":"Part 1: Schur–Weyl decomposition (shares H). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L337-L337","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.KnotEigenbasisData","kind":"structure","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L326-L370","doc":"**Completeness of the knot-type eigenbasis** (full data bundle).\n\nCombines:\n1. q-Schur–Weyl decomposition (semisimplicity of H_n(q))\n2. Alexander surjectivity (braid closure covers all links)\n3. Markov trace detection (every summand reached by some braid)\n\nTogether, these establish that knot types form a complete eigenbasis\nfor the algebraic direct limit `V_phys = colim V^⊗n`, replacing\nFeynman's continuum integral with a finite algebraic trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.mu_free_detection_vacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.mu_free_detection_vacuous","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L310-L324","doc":"**The μ-free detection shape asserts nothing per summand.**\n\nA single non-zero value `f β₀ ≠ 0` discharges\n\n    ∀ μ ∈ l, ∃ β, f β ≠ 0\n\nfor **every** list `l` of partitions, because `μ` does not occur in the body.\nThis is the shape `summands_detected` had until 2026-09-03, and it is\nrecorded as a theorem so the module docstring's claim about it is checked\nrather than asserted — and so a later \"simplification\" back to that shape\nfails against a standing demonstration of its emptiness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.markov_stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.markov_stab","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L304-L304","doc":"**Markov property** (Markov II / stabilisation):\ntr(x · T_{n-1}) = z · tr(x). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.tr_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.tr_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L301-L301","doc":"Non-degeneracy: the trace of the unit is non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.z_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.z_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L299-L299","doc":"z ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.z","kind":"def","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L297-L297","doc":"Markov parameter z determined by q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.trace_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.trace_comm","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L295-L295","doc":"Trace property (cyclicity / Markov I): tr(ab) = tr(ba). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.tr","kind":"def","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L293-L293","doc":"The trace functional tr : H_n(q) → ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L291-L291","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTrace","kind":"structure","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L282-L306","doc":"**Markov trace** on the Hecke algebra tower ⋃_n H_n(q).\nThe unique trace satisfying the Markov property\ntr(x σ_n^{±1}) = z^{±1} tr(x) for x ∈ H_n(q).\n\nOn each irreducible summand S_λ, the trace restricts to a non-zero\nscalar multiple of the character, so every summand is detected by\nsome braid closure. The trace value equals the Jones polynomial\nJ_L(q) of the braid closure up to a framing factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.alexander_has_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.alexander_has_braid","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L275-L278","doc":"Alexander surjectivity implies every link has a braid representative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.surjective","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L273-L273","doc":"**Surjectivity**: every link is the closure of some braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.closure","kind":"def","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L270-L270","doc":"Braid closure map β ↦ β̂. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.Braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.Braid","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L268-L268","doc":"Type of braids (union over all B_n). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.Link","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.Link","kind":"def","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L266-L266","doc":"Type of oriented links in S³. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L264-L264","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AlexanderSurjectivity","kind":"structure","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L257-L273","doc":"**Alexander's theorem**: every oriented link in S³ is the closure\nβ̂ of some braid β ∈ B_n for some n.\n\nThis guarantees surjectivity of the braid-closure map onto link types,\nwhich is essential for ensuring that the knot-type eigenbasis reaches\nevery irreducible summand of V^⊗n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.num_summands_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.num_summands_bound","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L249-L253","doc":"The number of partitions of n with ≤ 2 parts is ⌊n/2⌋ + 1.\nThis is a consequence of `partitions_count` on `SchurWeylDecomposition`:\nthe partition [a, b] with a + b = n, a ≥ b gives one summand per\nvalue of b = 0, 1, ..., ⌊n/2⌋. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.complete","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L246-L246","doc":"**Completeness**: every element of V^⊗n lies in the image of\nsome summand embedding. This encodes semisimplicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.summand_embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.summand_embed","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L241-L241","doc":"Embedding of each summand V_μ ⊗ S_μ into V^⊗n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.S_irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.S_irrep","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L239-L239","doc":"Irreducible H_n(q)-module for partition μ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.V_irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.V_irrep","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L237-L237","doc":"Irreducible SU_q(2)-module for partition μ (spin j). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_count","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L235-L235","doc":"The number of partitions equals ⌊n/2⌋ + 1 (one per spin value). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_valid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_valid","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L233-L233","doc":"Each partition has size n with at most 2 parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L231-L231","doc":"The set of partitions indexing the decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.tensorPower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.tensorPower","kind":"def","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L229-L229","doc":"Type of the tensor power V^⊗n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.n_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.n_eq","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L227-L227","doc":"Consistency: same n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.hecke","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L225-L225","doc":"The Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.n","kind":"def","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L223-L223","doc":"Number of tensor factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L221-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SchurWeylDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L210-L247","doc":"**q-Schur–Weyl decomposition** of V^⊗n under the joint action\nof SU_q(2) and the Hecke algebra H_n(q).\n\nWhen q is not a root of unity:\n  V^⊗n ≅ ⊕_{λ ⊢ n, ≤ 2 parts} V_λ ⊗ S_λ\nwhere V_λ is the irreducible SU_q(2)-module of spin j = (λ₁−λ₂)/2\nand S_λ is the irreducible H_n(q)-module.\n\nThe `complete` field encodes that the direct sum is exhaustive:\nevery element of V^⊗n lies in some summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.max_spin_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.max_spin_bound","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L182-L206","doc":"The maximum spin of a partition of n is n/2 (the fully symmetric case). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.spin_nonneg_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.spin_nonneg_single","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L178-L180","doc":"Spin labels are non-negative for single-part partitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.spin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.spin","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L169-L176","doc":"The spin label j = (λ₁ − λ₂)/2 for a two-part partition.\nThis is the spin of the irreducible SU_q(2)-module V_λ — a\nq-independent half-integer, hence valued in `ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.sorted","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L167-L167","doc":"Non-increasing (valid Young diagram). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.parts_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.parts_bound","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L165-L165","doc":"At most maxParts rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.size_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.size_eq","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L163-L163","doc":"The rows sum to n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.maxParts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.maxParts","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L161-L161","doc":"Maximum number of parts (rows). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.n","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L159-L159","doc":"Size n (sum of row lengths). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.rows","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L157-L157","doc":"Row lengths in non-increasing order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L155-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.BoundedPartition","kind":"structure","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L153-L167","doc":"A partition of n with at most r parts, represented as a\nnon-increasing list of row lengths. For SU_q(2), r = 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L148-L148","doc":"Quadratic relation: T_i² − (q − q⁻¹)·T_i − 1 = 0.\nEquivalently (T_i − q)(T_i + q⁻¹) = 0: eigenvalues are q and −q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.braid_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.braid_relation","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L142-L142","doc":"Braid relation: T_i T_{i+1} T_i = T_{i+1} T_i T_{i+1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.T","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L140-L140","doc":"Generators T₁, …, T_{n-1} (images of Artin generators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.smul","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L138-L138","doc":"Scalar multiplication by ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.sub","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L136-L136","doc":"Subtraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.zero","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L134-L134","doc":"Zero element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.one","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L132-L132","doc":"Unit element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.mul","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L130-L130","doc":"Multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.q_mul_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.q_mul_inv","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L126-L126","doc":"Defining relation `q · q⁻¹ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.q_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.q_inv","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L124-L124","doc":"Inverse parameter q⁻¹ (the ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` has no native\n`Inv`, so the inverse is carried as data). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L121-L121","doc":"q ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.q","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L119-L119","doc":"Deformation parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.carrier","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L117-L117","doc":"Carrier type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.n","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L115-L115","doc":"Number of strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeAlgebra","kind":"structure","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L107-L149","doc":"**Hecke algebra H_n(q)**: the quotient of the group algebra k[B_n]\nby the quadratic relation (σ_i − q)(σ_i + q⁻¹) = 0.\n\nWhen q is not a root of unity, H_n(q) is semisimple and isomorphic\nto k[S_n] as an abstract algebra (Jimbo's theorem). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.q_param","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.R_q","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete.lean#L99-L101","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}